# Dependencies
# No trailing slash: a Workflow-4 worktree symlinks node_modules into the
# primary checkout's install, and git sees a symlink as a FILE, which a
# directory-only "node_modules/" rule does not match (it would then be staged
# by `git add -A`). Matching the bare name covers the directory and the symlink.
node_modules

# Playwright run outputs & artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/

# AXI-2318 — prod E2E daily suite run outputs. The report is committed only by
# the workflow's commit job, under reports/AXI-2318/<date>-prod-daily-<runId>/.
/prod-suite-report/
/bundle/

# Campaign reports are committed under reports/<JIRA-ID>/ (owner rule
# 2026-10-25: reports live here, never on claude.ai artifacts). Re-include the
# Playwright outputs there, but never traces: a trace.zip records the test
# user's bearer token in its network log (NFR6).
!/reports/**/test-results/
!/reports/**/playwright-report/
/reports/**/trace.zip
/reports/**/playwright-report/data/*.zip

# AXI-1614 — raw shadow-run rows (a live-run artifact the aggregation script
# consumes; the generated report itself is committed under axiome-docs, this
# raw JSON is not)
tests/AXI-1462/harness/shadow-run/

# Auth storage state (per-role storageState — never committed; NFR6)
.auth/
storage-state*.json

# Local environment overrides (secrets never committed; NFR6)
.env
.env.local

# Staging action->route audit output (AXI-1369) — regenerated by
# `npm run stage:audit` against a live instance; a committed snapshot would go
# stale the moment a later story closes a gap, so it is a run artifact like
# test-results/, not source.
staging/audit/action-route-audit.json
staging/audit/action-route-audit.md

# Capture harness output (AXI-1381) — the master PNGs and run summary are
# regenerated by `npm run capture` against a live tenant; same reasoning as
# the audit artifact above (a committed PNG would go stale the moment the
# tenant is rebuilt, and would bloat repo history on every re-capture). The
# harness SOURCE under capture/masters/*.ts is tracked; only its *.png/.json
# run outputs are not.
capture/masters/*.png
capture/masters/summary.json
